      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n\n    int i, j, x, y;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        for (j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n            int insert_at = k;\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp simd reduction(min:insert_at)\n            for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\n                    if (x < insert_at) {\n                        insert_at = x;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n#else\n            for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\n                    insert_at = x;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n#endif\n\n            if (insert_at < k) {\n                for (y = k - 1; y > insert_at; y--) {\n                    distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                    labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n                }\n\n                distances[insert_at] = d;\n                labels[insert_at] = g.label;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n\n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "On builds enabling OpenMP SIMD, the read-only search for the first eligible top-k distance slot can use a min-index SIMD reduction, reducing the serial comparison chain. The subsequent insertion and shifts remain serial because they update dependent arrays.",
  "notes": "The reduction selects the lowest matching index, preserving strict-distance and encounter-order tie behavior. Builds without OpenMP retain the original early-exit scalar search. This is a performance hypothesis; no candidate was run.",
